    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.58) and **Junior Caminero** (80.71). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier play, benefiting from an elite .476 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Trey Yesavage; his combination of power and order placement makes him a foundational piece. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** earns a significant boost from a high-park-factor environment, pairing his .373 xwOBA with a favorable platoon advantage against Hughes. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** also command attention in the mid-70s range, both capitalizing on an excellent order-spot synergy and a beneficial platoon matchup against the left-handed Carson Palmquist.\n\nOur most critical decision involved **Nelson Velazquez**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a 48.11 score. While his platoon edge against Ryan Weathers was notable, he ultimately lacked the superior efficiency metrics of our outfield starters, particularly **Lars Nootbaar**, whose matchup against the vulnerable Randy V\u00e1squez yielded a strong 67.77 score thanks to a massive 19% SP skill advantage. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Josh Smith**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Lars Nootbaar**; should these projections deviate significantly once official orders are posted, the efficiency floor for **Gary Sanchez**\u2014currently at 40.66\u2014is at risk, specifically against the arm talent of Jared Jones. Finally, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** holds high speed-based upside, his benching is a direct result of a brutal 2.67 xERA matchup against Tarik Skubal, forcing us to prioritize safer, high-floor options like **Chase Meidroth** and **Caleb Durbin** to preserve our category integrity.",
